{"id":"d885c6dedea5ccf1fd029337efa0f8845dfc1bcc4efb019ed6499cefd7032e30","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:31Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["cbb9cf5f1f392165552df932e01b9e969f1deff08aba37d4bbfed5e748632483"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.Ip","hash":"59d0f6ef"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip","hash":"528b6d20"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1's own claim is the prefix range per family: parse_cidr/1 accepts /0 and /32 for IPv4 and refuses /33 and /-1; accepts ::/0 and ::/128 and refuses ::/129. The rest of §1 names the types, which the type class excuses.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"07e309de87cac9ae8a38b22e478cfda41972da74ace5636892351374f4a8cc69","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:37Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["58a9aa790a6b70aa1d3cfe7c37c78d502ac117910725839410ad66116874a089"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: parse/1 gives the address, trimmed and normalized, or nil","hash":"eb36e9e5"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#ip-parse","hash":"5f53ae82"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Each case of the hint is one assertion: 203.0.113.9 to its tuple, ' 2001:db8::42 ' (padded) to the IPv6 tuple, ::ffff:203.0.113.5 to {203, 0, 113, 5}, and not-an-ip, the shortened 10.1 and the empty string to nil.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"db3323aa4b30b7d75b76fd327f92f41db3e11a6b374ef8444c18546fe392ec5d","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:39Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["cf767045a9ef199ddb873d21c9cf1536e079788f7e8eabdcdd3b9dc38d4376f9"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: parse/1 never raises on a string: it gives a normalized address or nil","hash":"2805a5cc"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-parse","hash":"445f9df9"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.1's own claim beyond the hint is that parse/1 never raises on a string and returns the address normalized or nil: the property feeds printable strings and address-like strings (digits, hex, dots, colons, spaces, slashes) and asserts each result is nil or an :inet address equal to its own normalize/1.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"e61f9d35e64af4190601dce7b31b884b8b1d4f1580dae88aa81b675ee25341bc","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:39Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["b19c0300d4a7c2b244f4b2d95e1a2cad165c5c64149e315ed1c340d87a410fa5"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.Ip.parse/1","hash":"e397fdd3"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-parse","hash":"445f9df9"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.1's own claim beyond the hint is that parse/1 never raises on a string and returns the address normalized or nil: the property feeds printable strings and address-like strings (digits, hex, dots, colons, spaces, slashes) and asserts each result is nil or an :inet address equal to its own normalize/1.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"a64a5674c051efa5fd8cb60bff07bd4aec7227f2c6c56118ea66982d29888986","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:41Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["390b730fa066647b7e1825a3c45393e63d643b76f6828321d5849d3554247ab4"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: parse_cidr/1 gives each row of the spec's table","hash":"1a13d460"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#ip-parse-cidr","hash":"605138c4"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Every row of §1.2's table is an exact assertion (192.0.2.1 to /32, 2001:db8::/32, the out-of-range, not-a-number, host-name and 1/2/3 errors with their quoting messages), plus the hint's single IPv6 address as a /128 (2001:db8::1), which the table lacks.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"7bfd722da1df0280364e7d9886ea1e1ff6092c896b1a6294c16bd1970c7b1f76","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:43Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["e6b461653c48eb187891bdebcaae8fa86f765f8409524a61bfc203334a20c3b1"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: parse_cidr/1 trims, keeps the network as written, and takes only a whole decimal prefix","hash":"2e039d48"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-parse-cidr","hash":"b07c591c"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.2's bullets beyond the table: ' 10.1.2.3/8 ' is trimmed and kept as {{10, 1, 2, 3}, 8}, and matching masks it (10.200.0.1 in, 11.1.2.3 out); 8.0 and an empty prefix are not whole numbers; /129 is outside IPv6's 0..128; every error quotes the input.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"80c0234950f70e16ded6eda6f59fdc004d186b8d047bb022463b4ff26128cd97","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:43Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["71195bf173a5dbb753592fb75f89d360cbac1aaa4bc0714c8c683fed1fc00f77"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.Ip.parse_cidr/1","hash":"436e106e"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-parse-cidr","hash":"b07c591c"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.2's bullets beyond the table: ' 10.1.2.3/8 ' is trimmed and kept as {{10, 1, 2, 3}, 8}, and matching masks it (10.200.0.1 in, 11.1.2.3 out); 8.0 and an empty prefix are not whole numbers; /129 is outside IPv6's 0..128; every error quotes the input.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"9f904d81681a32515e4e120b07b57da8e93974c8914fb4161631b5f24cf8aeb1","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:47Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["c74c970a3a4c5902a8957bb5be5869ca49bfc980b8acd5a86449bdb3d1fd20fc"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: normalize/1 turns an IPv4-mapped address into IPv4 and returns any other unchanged","hash":"bb99a6fb"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#ip-normalize","hash":"711d5e3f"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint's three cases, one assertion each: {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0xFFFF, 0x0A00, 0x0005} normalizes to {10, 0, 0, 5}; the IPv4 tuple 203.0.113.9 and the IPv6 tuple 2001:db8::42 come back unchanged.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"8ee75ddc4efd016b97c886032d8b30ea02b2ba4fef6d5806234496a843f23d08","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:49Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["9c4413b33b226df777afbd6945638e83c2b8ab379ee90da78cb149cd6cc88377"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: an address is in a CIDR of its own family; in_any?/2 normalizes first","hash":"2cc9af8f"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#ip-membership","hash":"43eabfda"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint's four claims: 10.9.9.9 is in 10.0.0.0/8 and not in 11.0.0.0/8; it is not in the IPv6 ::/0 (no IPv6 CIDR can hold it); ::ffff:10.9.9.9 is in 10.0.0.0/8 through in_any?/2; in_any?/2 with no CIDRs is false.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"39ab058851b38e7184e081d5755bf222b9308876c629ed0865e5744468929810","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:52Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["95860c5894b21113a1a0bd0c82339317d573c67744923ff181eac5c8570fe309"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: the first prefix bits decide; a /0 holds its whole family and no other","hash":"37a99066"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-membership","hash":"2c3587e2"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.4's own claims: the first prefix bits decide (10.127.255.255 in 10.0.0.0/9, 10.128.0.0 not: the ninth bit); a /0 matches every address of its family and families never match (property: any IPv4 in an IPv4 /0 and not in ::/0, any IPv6 in an IPv6 /0 and not in 0.0.0.0/0); in_any?/2 is true when any CIDR holds it.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"6b64f794523a17194c768573ba3712d63ee08a518ec2c4977b0ca5905dbbcaf6","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:52Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["e5ae6f02e1932a3de735b1084e261b24784f0c0c78b754f6d8039d40e62c5992"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.Ip.in_any?/2","hash":"d2874d65"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-membership","hash":"2c3587e2"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.4's own claims: the first prefix bits decide (10.127.255.255 in 10.0.0.0/9, 10.128.0.0 not: the ninth bit); a /0 matches every address of its family and families never match (property: any IPv4 in an IPv4 /0 and not in ::/0, any IPv6 in an IPv6 /0 and not in 0.0.0.0/0); in_any?/2 is true when any CIDR holds it.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"77f514d719b4ab37607fefca70ab280bdc9a43975ca4d9bca2659d02649e321a","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:52Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["13c74020ab2851a0a0ad103f60d8788574bae39c3aaba610ae7d744054685607"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.Ip.in_cidr?/2","hash":"4f1d9721"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-membership","hash":"2c3587e2"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.4's own claims: the first prefix bits decide (10.127.255.255 in 10.0.0.0/9, 10.128.0.0 not: the ninth bit); a /0 matches every address of its family and families never match (property: any IPv4 in an IPv4 /0 and not in ::/0, any IPv6 in an IPv6 /0 and not in 0.0.0.0/0); in_any?/2 is true when any CIDR holds it.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"8a2604fc99e0479124c1da2bda6cc15f953b013ac28cf9a7049327b306a49737","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:54Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["03d96008a4d608dc9347860b906af9061e86cfaa2ddece06e2f7067356477364"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: to_string/1 formats as :inet.ntoa/1 does","hash":"e9341171"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-to-string","hash":"f553102a"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.5's own claim, the format: {203, 0, 113, 9} is 203.0.113.9 and the IPv6 tuple is the compressed 2001:db8::42, the section's two examples exactly.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"91bc535afeebb8ab0fd5ecbc8af9751c89c1cad2e08036fa85a2befe39cccb90","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:54Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["db90178599ac79042ba5c6bf7c3c7a01bd3c3116b063303aa4d67cc9a094c545"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.Ip.to_string/1","hash":"c89f07d0"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-ip-to-string","hash":"f553102a"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.5's own claim, the format: {203, 0, 113, 9} is 203.0.113.9 and the IPv6 tuple is the compressed 2001:db8::42, the section's two examples exactly.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"27e4588af2b45097dc4f7071546f9a44b0a4c473c524ee06a19b878dd18c76b3","at":"2026-10-27T04:48:55Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["d13893c686f9e8d79572513ee5ebff129470c8cea59db8af9c44b11f2520d8c6"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: addresses: to_string/1 then parse/1 gives the address back","hash":"4dee5d61"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#ip-to-string","hash":"d6b49c03"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint's identity as a property: for generated IPv4 tuples and IPv6 tuples, excluding IPv4-mapped ones as the hint does, parse(to_string(ip)) == ip.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"dff5d4cdd9f37862ac494e08a98cd1f30afe0d2a4bae85ecffc53a0611223fbc","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:01Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["42e0dea44ea82dca36b6ce17591625b9ea6b07a40d5ff9b93ce23e0531bc4356"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: trusted peer: several headers are read in order; empty entries are dropped","hash":"dccbbffa"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#client-ip-several-headers","hash":"421e03e8"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Both halves of the hint: two x-forwarded-for headers, 198.51.100.7 then 203.0.113.9, behind trusted 10.0.0.5 resolve to 203.0.113.9 (read in the other order the client would be 198.51.100.7); forwarded_for/1 of 'a, ,b' is [a, b]. Extended in this adoption with the forwarded_for/1 assertion.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"f7a6f5fead8eab74a25287a72d2563fe6303b6173259a578a10bc09c62f97636","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:02Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["19a387aeca342a1adb805816227762efee1603328b4518d2add8673c170bfd8c"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: trusted peer: forwarded_for/1: every header in order, split on commas, trimmed, empties dropped","hash":"cf48fa7b"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-forwarded","hash":"e0d49e7e"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§2.1's sentence, clause by clause: headers ' a ,b,' then ', c' give [a, b, c] (both headers, in order received, split on commas, each trimmed, the trailing and leading empty entries dropped); a request without the header gives [].","basis":"review"}
{"id":"080ae7f74fa7b01f1b60e89f6830b07a8530e65af2a2efce3190ec03f9a7a22a","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:02Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["2d834f99003f3d632aaf56c3fb2973609a0fda95933517f9ed47c98a8ec7db22"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIp.forwarded_for/1","hash":"061cb822"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-forwarded","hash":"e0d49e7e"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§2.1's sentence, clause by clause: headers ' a ,b,' then ', c' give [a, b, c] (both headers, in order received, split on commas, each trimmed, the trailing and leading empty entries dropped); a request without the header gives [].","basis":"review"}
{"id":"0e9d0ea15fa5f5f0a6c3049d1f9034ff217d9c3cdd181a039b84e645e97c0c89","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:04Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["9f2859890c50743dfc74e2952e91eeb83d652efd25dbc6b522a63ab3988982c9"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: trusted peer: resolve/3: no entries give the peer; peer, entries and client are compared normalized","hash":"c303bf4b"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-rule","hash":"26ebd290"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Two §2 bullets no row covers: no entries gives the peer (10.0.0.5 with []); normalization of peer, entries and result (a mapped peer with no entries gives {10, 0, 0, 5}; a mapped trusted entry ::ffff:10.1.1.1 is skipped as trusted; a mapped client entry comes back as IPv4).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"a686f7e3e83ab74b927d5284d3209ac3ffde28f1ab709da95a58324b8cb27fcf","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:04Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["c9acd39aa30dce42db28128ab66259a4d61eb421b1acf50d864bff305b0d0f5a"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIp.resolve/3","hash":"5960ab27"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-rule","hash":"26ebd290"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Two §2 bullets no row covers: no entries gives the peer (10.0.0.5 with []); normalization of peer, entries and result (a mapped peer with no entries gives {10, 0, 0, 5}; a mapped trusted entry ::ffff:10.1.1.1 is skipped as trusted; a mapped client entry comes back as IPv4).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"fe8447c6cc09b6d13b1052e63daa3bffd2de2dbcbc99577a84e7f4e5002624ff","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:05Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["f38ca3177cc610c920642fae21c3bba673c90022b2acd870fb07c07998ec4790"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: the spec's table: each row, with 10.0.0.0/8 and fd00::/8 trusted","hash":"b45aa9e5"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#client-ip-rows","hash":"b4f92342"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"All seven rows of §2's table, peer, header and client copied from it, run through the plug with exactly 10.0.0.0/8 and fd00::/8 trusted; each assertion names its row's peer and header when it fails.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"96d81f990a67c8d4d318f105cf31acf09d6d3863ce5c9cdb6e0292e8a4f6aeed","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:08Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["291dde199e7e465ea94a082ca079312562ad83c0e4fcc00632987a56d6a1bdff"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: untrusted peer: only a non-empty header from an untrusted peer emits, with the peer normalized","hash":"a6ff70c8"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-event","hash":"3009c70f"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's own claims beyond its hint: a header of empty entries only emits nothing (' , ' from untrusted 198.51.100.9); a forwarded request from a trusted peer emits nothing; the metadata peer is normalized (mapped ::ffff:198.51.100.10 arrives as {198, 51, 100, 10}) and the request is served with the header ignored (remote_ip is the peer). refute_received checks no other event was emitted.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"e47fcc4dafb9debb57430ce54f9e233fc85d9c2bf800276f1271e72457ca34fc","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:09Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["3ba411e3690851e40c068046d3b717bb7e3ae21d19b3622c42caa8a2d07b457e"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: what the plug sets: remote_ip is the client and peer/1 the socket peer; without the plug, peer/1 is remote_ip","hash":"a68c736d"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#client-ip-peer","hash":"f7c7f1e9"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint's two cases: after the plug, a trusted 10.0.0.5 forwarding for 203.0.113.9 has remote_ip {203, 0, 113, 9} and peer/1 {10, 0, 0, 5}; a conn the plug never ran on (remote_ip 192.0.2.1) has peer/1 equal to its remote_ip.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"c3976542c8d96dc312433902a25db10f0c6711ae9cad3a972e6ed5304bee700d","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:16Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["d71daf5fab1864968a0d613b92cc9f46211fd4aaa18489c193ac505674dea64a"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: what the plug sets: the client is written in remote_ip only; the peer, normalized, in private","hash":"a9df670d"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-call","hash":"720b806d"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§4's three bullets and its 'written once' sentence: a mapped trusted peer forwarding for 203.0.113.9 gets remote_ip {203, 0, 113, 9}, conn.private.macaw_plug_peer {10, 0, 0, 5} (normalized), and no assigns; a forwarded request from untrusted 198.51.100.7 emits the untrusted-forward event. peer/1 is checked by client-ip-peer.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"380bf6b9fb57735477ae4701859c857cacbe2fab575b8ac83ed9ce59c92ccf49","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:17Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["b0722df1b10797833c36a2b722c00c7fa1761f160d1211d6b0a72e74064573bf"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: configuration: a list takes {address, prefix} tuples as they are; any other entry raises at init, or is dropped from a dynamic list","hash":"38c7d559"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-config","hash":"8cac4721"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§3's claims beyond its four hints: a static {address, prefix} tuple is taken as is (10.0.0.0/8 as a tuple trusts 10.0.0.5); a malformed string raises with the exact 'trusted_proxies: ' prefix on parse_cidr/1's message; an entry of another shape (42) raises 'trusted_proxies: 42 is not an address or a CIDR'; in a dynamic list a tuple is taken and 42 is dropped, the request resolved against the rest, and bad_proxy_entry carries entry 42 and its reason. The default logger's message for it is checked under §5.1.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"d301d23d47abb021c0baf8dabc54bd7b68aad6e0f1a523c41f5bb4bb1d37277c","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:19Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["bd56632b938915ba85ffd8b26a7fe360de04d04279bba1937637e00f9c178983"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: the default logger: each event logs its own message once per interval, concurrent events once; a second attach is refused","hash":"8b18c333"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-logger","hash":"9fcc18f5"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5.1's claims: attach returns :ok, then {:error, :already_exists}; 50 concurrent untrusted forwards from 198.51.100.7 log the untrusted message exactly once (CAS), and that first one logs at once; a bad dynamic entry logs its own message, exact text with the entry and reason, once over two requests, separately from the untrusted slot (it logs although the untrusted slot already fired). The exact warning texts are asserted whole.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"5ba94831003fe49f62cd3d76bd3d1ea7b09b1f85d44b1f1dce9212ca54c97dec","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:19Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["f5ff4d78e0ef59673c92660162f14efc96eb57614eff5143f4a77a46cfb4f5af"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIp.attach_default_logger/1","hash":"cebb991a"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-logger","hash":"9fcc18f5"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5.1's claims: attach returns :ok, then {:error, :already_exists}; 50 concurrent untrusted forwards from 198.51.100.7 log the untrusted message exactly once (CAS), and that first one logs at once; a bad dynamic entry logs its own message, exact text with the entry and reason, once over two requests, separately from the untrusted slot (it logs although the untrusted slot already fired). The exact warning texts are asserted whole.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"f7396c3c04214f47fbe872be29bea69a2944621fe0c2a0552e1361421d0408bb","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:23Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["3fc36ad521d6e32e662492b8702b0c59598faafb468f8cb2370182d46161e381"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: the interval is period / count in whole µs, at least 1; a refusal costs nothing; an idle key has its burst","hash":"aca4d296"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-gcra","hash":"b9e08603"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1's bullets beyond its hints: interval = period/count in whole µs ({3, :second} gives 333_333) and at least 1 ({2_000_000, :second}); tolerance (burst-1) x interval (666_666); a never-seen key is allowed with TAT now + interval (the row holds 1 s); five refusals leave the TAT unchanged and the next slot opens exactly at 1 s; after a burst of 3, a key idle 1 s has its full burst of 3 again and no more.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"cc925a55a0bbb8501eaf5e46d4b8ef21d9ea04084658efca0278880ca4d81473","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:24Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["da15efd16c1a2713c24187f5781f0e76079e9dbe7ae8a4ab23892355edd79774"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: check reads the monotonic clock by default, and rounds a wait up to a whole second","hash":"c2ca1b11"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-check","hash":"b0cc0314"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§3's claims beyond rate-wait: check/2 reads the monotonic clock (allowed, then {:error, 60} for {1, :minute}); a wait is rounded up, never down: 30 s + 1 µs to wait gives 31, 29.5 s gives 30. The table requirement is checked by the TableTest test tagged with this section.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"1ce47259b98e9949f881019f0a2829e8dc03e5624076453d471dce83afb3d12d","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:24Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["66736e2cc1b0e8e44882f075a23902b250f75287b830457dfa070769836731c8"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.check/3","hash":"8c7cf9ac"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-check","hash":"b0cc0314"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§3's claims beyond rate-wait: check/2 reads the monotonic clock (allowed, then {:error, 60} for {1, :minute}); a wait is rounded up, never down: 30 s + 1 µs to wait gives 31, 29.5 s gives 30. The table requirement is checked by the TableTest test tagged with this section.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"c1417e15b1c540b75d2ee65f46d44ca94637a44275f15198054deb98e5dc0a95","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:30Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["7c346c44a27cb9955e407d9fa522d85a208fb4ee6097567408b0562ab1275ee6"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: a limiter: named by any term, never sharing a key with another; rate required; burst count by default","hash":"76bec6cd"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-new","hash":"08ba466f"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§2's claims beyond rate-new-raises: ids are any term (tuples with a string) and two limiters never share a key (:k allowed on both at once, then refused on the first); burst defaults to count (3 allowed at once for {3, :second}, the 4th refused); rate is required (KeyError without it); a non-integer count is refused; the two messages are asserted whole.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"6107990c3a206fce8d5fd4cc765b20192d085574977fd626c07a4aac6cb6ce50","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:30Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["d79884aedd63d8918e62b577cd83094952bc95c549af251372716aff871baa1d"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.new/2","hash":"d81af0d8"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-new","hash":"08ba466f"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§2's claims beyond rate-new-raises: ids are any term (tuples with a string) and two limiters never share a key (:k allowed on both at once, then refused on the first); burst defaults to count (3 allowed at once for {3, :second}, the 4th refused); rate is required (KeyError without it); a non-integer count is refused; the two messages are asserted whole.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"8fc7d9545741436fdbee14a8854daeafbe4ed821f614943dbd46310cbfb2c96a","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:31Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["0344596af2a267effb07d320edb58efd4764462aba89ed97977179fd3df89544"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: concurrent first requests on a new key: one inserts the row, the rest decide again against it","hash":"f628e79a"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-cas","hash":"45b0cec8"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1.1's first-row claim, which rate-concurrent (burst 25) can't isolate: 200 concurrent first checks of a new key at one instant with burst 1 allow exactly one (only one insert succeeds); the other 199 decide again against the inserted row and are refused with the full hour; the row holds that one TAT.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"a3100870035d82df04d730b4729455732e18964f1f83234d25391a7c9f3e2bd4","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:33Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["1965d6c84a918cfac488aedb54e458f18af98f837b7f937524c2cbddd3342459"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: the plug: an allowed request passes unchanged; a refused one is answered in plain text, or by on_limit after retry-after is set, and halted","hash":"bc30ed1f"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-plug","hash":"bc7219cf"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§4's claims beyond its two hints: an allowed request's conn is returned equal to the input; the default refusal is sent, 429, content-type text/plain, body 'Too many requests; retry in 60 s.' with its newline, halted; with on_limit the retry-after header is already 60 when the function runs (it echoes it) and the conn is halted; :id is required (KeyError).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"d459bbef7bcb67750a00d3732dc40cf33fcae5cdb3751ad74f6547ebb1c37c7a","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:34Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["c7b0b02888100c87385fd4709f6ae42edbf82bb59b431b36a32e2f2005181dad"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: the plug: the :now function is read at each call, not at init","hash":"0af0c6ef"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#rate-clock-per-call","hash":"e51940b7"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint exactly: one init/1 result, a :now function over a counter, rate {1, :minute}; the first call passes, the counter advances a minute, the second call through the same init result passes too (a clock read at init would refuse it).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"862b96a89ee295d78106e87c4f6736f2247a62aad27de57c8c1b37b5b62e73ca","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:36Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["488888bc0d07b5dcfd71b0a9cf482a947c1550a327f9987de3a745506d2a0b13"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimitTest: the plug: init/1 keeps the clock unread: :monotonic by default, read by call/2","hash":"419e8bae"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-clock","hash":"5fb05c86"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§4.1's own claim: init/1 keeps the clock as given, the function itself or :monotonic by default, never a time; with the default, call/2 reads the monotonic clock per request (the first passes, the second is refused with 429).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"6ad7f26ac124f15a2bce3d02ac2425b18d32e8a04ae17182bf61bd66a42c0008","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:37Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["3eecc291163b0ef1b52b7b2dbf26d21da3abd1d1b902d3dfaed641f0b3de7280"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.TableTest: check needs the table running; without it, it raises","hash":"5d6643e3"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-check","hash":"b0cc0314"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§3's last sentence: with the table not running (asserted first), check/3 raises ArgumentError; once the table is started it answers :ok. A sync module, so no async test loses the table.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"5c890771abe9dd39e1078b6f9ba608dc1589033b38ccdb32019f29804409818b","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:43Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["a08832a1d93b1a7658788119681384d414416cb855c51d85bb993241b3440428"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.TableTest: the table: named, public, a set with read and write concurrency; a sweep counts what it deletes; a restart starts empty","hash":"cd1944a5"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-table","hash":"a0865d91"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's claims: the table is owned by the process registered under the module's name, and is named, public, a set with read and write concurrency (ets:info); the sweep interval defaults to 60_000 ms (the server's state); sweep(5 s) deletes the two rows with TAT 1 s and returns 2, then 0; a swept key is decided as never seen (allowed); a restart starts empty and the 10 s key has its burst again. The sweep-check race itself is not deterministic and is not exercised; its outcome (a gone row decided as new) is.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"0916ee06f3182e9698c1c5ea7b55c768d26257f261d97d65b0737b33cda195ba","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:43Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["82e6c5f3f3d96f1d864d1ffedd6b611bd78c772f26764841bc3ac54a690d9160"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.Table","hash":"dc9b8e4b"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-table","hash":"a0865d91"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's claims: the table is owned by the process registered under the module's name, and is named, public, a set with read and write concurrency (ets:info); the sweep interval defaults to 60_000 ms (the server's state); sweep(5 s) deletes the two rows with TAT 1 s and returns 2, then 0; a swept key is decided as never seen (allowed); a restart starts empty and the 10 s key has its burst again. The sweep-check race itself is not deterministic and is not exercised; its outcome (a gone row decided as new) is.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"58cc045a3cc33b527178427d450d2da7f768b10d30d017d0a41e80075b7764b5","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:43Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["c3c1f17f0bcedd4d25c73b7dfeff42da84d7d77062c956266a85855afaf9da17"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.Table.sweep/1","hash":"1cc8a68c"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-table","hash":"a0865d91"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's claims: the table is owned by the process registered under the module's name, and is named, public, a set with read and write concurrency (ets:info); the sweep interval defaults to 60_000 ms (the server's state); sweep(5 s) deletes the two rows with TAT 1 s and returns 2, then 0; a swept key is decided as never seen (allowed); a restart starts empty and the 10 s key has its burst again. The sweep-check race itself is not deterministic and is not exercised; its outcome (a gone row decided as new) is.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"02e78bad6a1892e274689462fe1e91cbe2161dbe50551648a19b855e27ba3c82","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:44Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["03d0b688af6cfee20a45ef2b30db69f837fc8d11fcb30c9f14d54d8c84f41cb2"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.TableTest: the table sweeps itself every :sweep_every milliseconds","hash":"748991fb"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-table","hash":"a0865d91"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's 'the table runs it every :sweep_every milliseconds': with sweep_every: 10 a row whose TAT passed 9 s ago is gone within a bounded poll (100 x 10 ms), with no sweep called by the test.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"18d2518782a17ed8d043a175a5d8ab955e867da65599372fcd12a993a56c7e58","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:51Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["fa66eeb680534592feaaf5bb68fdc1407f2621df64779d82fdfd9e80a7bf1d0c"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: policy/2 renders directives in order, as name and value, joined by \"; \"","hash":"833a4c41"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-policy","hash":"5f09d46e"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1's claims beyond its hint: policy/0 is the default string; policy/2 renders the directives given in their order, each 'name value' with _ as -, joined by '; ' (worker_src then img_src stay in that order, and no directive is invented); hashes go after script-src's value. Written in this adoption, it found policy/2 adding an empty script-src to directives that lack one; fixed in policy/2.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"5df47582d5f6d0fbbee88f5a1474ddee17fbd73b07a0cad01d3c43b6c7aad9fe","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:51Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["bb8adbe9fae32f315edd8dcea8a16ce1be08d262c4654aaa64f3eeab134cdb50"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeaders.policy/2","hash":"8c2b9afc"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-policy","hash":"5f09d46e"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§1's claims beyond its hint: policy/0 is the default string; policy/2 renders the directives given in their order, each 'name value' with _ as -, joined by '; ' (worker_src then img_src stay in that order, and no directive is invented); hashes go after script-src's value. Written in this adoption, it found policy/2 adding an empty script-src to directives that lack one; fixed in policy/2.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"24b489739d14260c6f49f066ef64e46a64672270da81d2d3b93cfb366dba7d16","at":"2026-10-27T04:49:56Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["e1ea0fbda8068d70d0ad2470631186b0a96a2940f6d178628d291981fb8c5344"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: the standard headers are on every response","hash":"bfb1eb35"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#headers-standard","hash":"4578f626"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint: with no options each of §6's five headers has its table value, asserted exactly; permissions-policy was checked only for camera=() before this adoption and is now the whole value.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"c1bad61184154ec13826443742b1364058135e9b9dc482752f66943ddbed96cc","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:01Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["90103cf2f7c20f7b0683bdeab1c05015da07edfc568e4a61158daab58c63fbee"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: every response carries the policy and the five standard headers","hash":"7da45236"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#headers-every-response","hash":"b29052b3"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint across responses: for GET, POST and DELETE, sent with 200, 302, 404 and 500, chunked and as a file, each response carries exactly one content-security-policy and one of each of §6's five headers.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"6cb8e7f68f9f8d75ffe2c5e318f0a121963a62a01b140d122c16aaf63d5f99b0","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:07Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["4d4245a28e273c89b92c684799dfcf984cd73a1a699aa55c13485b52b034d332"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: HSTS only over https","hash":"b244d9e2"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#headers-hsts","hash":"c0eebb41"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint's three cases: none over http; max-age=31536000 over https; none over https with hsts: nil (added in this adoption).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"4580cbbf932d02dd9faca8678c300261e6c283416a26dd1c1c436643cc24ada7","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:18Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["ddfb500f6b856c2b1c80717d3c3ccdbb754052844f43940bc65582ea4ee76f31"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: hsts: sets the default value or, not a string, turns it off; over http none, whatever headers: says","hash":"d870d136"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-hsts","hash":"2d304c42"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's claims beyond its hints: hsts: 'max-age=10' sets the https value; hsts: false (not a string) turns it off; over http there is none even when headers: names strict-transport-security or hsts: is set.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"c10be19d46a1507147adf081be5db3c7440b21f1e21b2d0e459e4f779e5bb757","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:25Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["9299d59101470ea7e7be945f75b74b05709961a0d03ddf4580f33e0aa02afb91"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: a directive changes only by naming it","hash":"36316de0"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#headers-override-in-place","hash":"adf918b9"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint: img_src's override appears in img-src's place, now asserted between style-src and font-src (extended in this adoption: it only checked presence before), and default-src is unchanged.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"e56ee71baaa3352b55d4610531372b5aff1c427a99381aa71d167a7eedd338dc","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:31Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["76deb73e382f8595a9443f42941fe9ec5842511c4fea990ba4ca61dc6f9d1504"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: a directive the defaults lack is added after them","hash":"37d4d958"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#headers-override-added","hash":"be1bab0e"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint exactly: csp: [worker_src: \"'self'\"] gives the whole policy equal to the ten defaults in order followed by '; worker-src 'self''.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"35849eda6ec098e1a48841b83b1afab07109c8e6c68860d3b860a4cc327563b6","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:36Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["7d54f94e595318e94c95e8ffa6a68968e72b659a9b43495a50af20e93011e90b"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: overrides keep one order, tighten or loosen as named, and must be {atom, string}","hash":"50693385"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-overrides","hash":"fecbdf25"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§2's claims beyond its hints: several overrides at once keep one order (default_src, script_src and frame_ancestors replaced where they stand, worker-src then manifest-src added after the defaults in the order given), the whole policy asserted; a loosening ('unsafe-inline') is taken as named; a nil value and a string key each raise the exact 'csp: <entry> is not {directive, value}' message.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"4ba378dc3a819e7044edac72037a35e7310096e4d5918e4a47aa7b62bad88ca7","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:42Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["22d631ba80bca6d35c4f4e29c0856caf89e09c35dfa46fc36380a6db6d8fe721"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: headers: adds a header the table lacks, beside the standard ones","hash":"2cf98e03"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-standard","hash":"564b51d6"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§6's claim beyond its two hints: a name not in the table (x-permitted-cross-domain-policies) adds a header, and the five standard headers are still sent beside it. Replacement and removal are checked by headers-replace-remove.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"0bd107f0e6a8fd63462877bb6d474ac0c5993ede9310db299d066bd2025e7cc1","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:48Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["b2288a9464933c46f60e26bd2d5b760a8d0a373232a154019ff1ca7ad1c12daa"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: nothing is written until the response is sent; then each header replaces a controller's value","hash":"36f8648c"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-call","hash":"841d6284"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§4's claims: after call/2 and before sending no policy and none of the five headers is set (register_before_send); a controller's x-frame-options SAMEORIGIN and content-security-policy 'default-src *' are replaced by DENY and the closed policy when the response is sent (put_resp_header, one value each).","basis":"review"}
{"id":"af08fb63fcc8af674441058dacb5340b786dc8a4f26f175a9e0235cae108231d","at":"2026-10-27T04:50:58Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["a2446b2b4f23f8bc108ccc5f337b9465de2584cead5c815fa1991972b833f9e0"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeadersTest: inline script hashes: a hash is of the body byte for byte; the list keeps first-added order, after script-src's value","hash":"d87216e9"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-hashes","hash":"a86086d0"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§3's claims beyond its hints: the hash is of the exact bytes (a leading space or a trailing semicolon changes it); hashes put b, a, b give b then a, once each, in first-added order; they follow script-src's whole value (\"'self' https://cdn.example\"); no 'unsafe-inline' is added. A hash put before the plug is kept, per §3's corrected last bullet, and checked by headers-hash-before-plug.","basis":"review"}
