{"id":"24f28c3ad32188ccd4ab33aa8ed8a4841d6ddbfd0d7f976c5a86200c67697232","at":"2026-10-27T04:53:55Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["af149fd9f1e79a51aaf0c3412777f721feb4da5e8555d84bca8561bb39bae550"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit","hash":"3dd230f6"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-plug","hash":"bc7219cf"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Read RateLimit's init/1, call/2 and limited/3 against §4: the test drives init/1 and call/2 and asserts the unchanged conn when allowed, the default 429 answer (retry-after, text/plain, the body, halted) from limited/3 with no on_limit, and the on_limit path seeing retry-after already set and halting; init/1 requires :id.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"e9e679cb3605e004c4a6c293a487dab71088f8111dc516b319bbc48caf85ca41","at":"2026-10-27T04:54:01Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["a133b72f26b482d2926214dd17f2d268b6ed6d0a74a62369af8b048d1209951c"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Macaw.Plug.SecurityHeaders","hash":"3bd4a780"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/03-security-headers.md#plug-headers-call","hash":"841d6284"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Read SecurityHeaders' init/1, call/2 and the before-send function against §4: the test drives init/1 and call/2, asserts nothing is set before sending (call/2 only registers), and that at send the policy and the headers are written with put_resp_header, replacing a controller's earlier x-frame-options and content-security-policy.","basis":"review"}
