{"id":"241cc98cc7dcc53506bc28cfaaec169f63c622673130ec7d2ab8343c877fc1b1","at":"2026-10-27T04:55:30Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["d301d23d47abb021c0baf8dabc54bd7b68aad6e0f1a523c41f5bb4bb1d37277c"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.ClientIpTest: the default logger: each event logs its own message once per interval, concurrent events once; a second attach is refused","hash":"92e69ad9"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/01-client-ip.md#plug-client-ip-logger","hash":"9fcc18f5"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5.1's claims, now with the default interval: attach_default_logger/0 (one minute) returns :ok and a second attach {:error, :already_exists}; 50 concurrent untrusted forwards log the exact untrusted warning once, the first at once (CAS); a bad dynamic entry logs its exact warning once over two requests, in its own slot.","basis":"review"}
