{"id":"2ede947f5b756c8f359998355c05936cf4128d18acebc7288f28c23de0555fa6","at":"2026-10-27T04:55:33Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["6ad7f26ac124f15a2bce3d02ac2425b18d32e8a04ae17182bf61bd66a42c0008"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.TableTest: check needs the table running; without it, it raises","hash":"6d9c3a0d"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-check","hash":"b0cc0314"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§3's last sentence: with the table not running (asserted first), check/3 raises ArgumentError; once the table is started (here by start_link/0, its defaults) it answers :ok.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"37bacf3013a956778b3101eb5cc7f25637c931a413052e8ae1c830a7ec5285e2","at":"2026-10-27T04:55:45Z","commit":"b9541d724f9b8e6bd225feeaf03ab95d61bbb76a","parents":["5c890771abe9dd39e1078b6f9ba608dc1589033b38ccdb32019f29804409818b"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Macaw.Plug.RateLimit.TableTest: the table: named, public, a set with read and write concurrency; a sweep counts what it deletes; a restart starts empty","hash":"046e7174"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/02-rate-limit.md#plug-rate-table","hash":"a0865d91"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"§5's claims: the table, started with its defaults, is owned by the process registered under the module's name and is named, public, a set with read and write concurrency; the sweep interval defaults to 60_000 ms (the server's state); sweep(5 s) deletes the two rows with TAT 1 s and returns 2, then 0; a swept key is decided as never seen; a restart starts empty; sweep/0 sweeps at the clock's now (of a row 9 s past and one 11 s ahead it deletes 1). The sweep-check race is not deterministic and isn't exercised; its outcome (a gone row decided as new) is.","basis":"review"}
